<title>SWITZERLAND: SBC lowers cash bond rates.</title>
<headline>SBC lowers cash bond rates.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp (SBC) said it was</p>
<p>lowering the interest rate it pays on cash bonds</p>
<p>(Kassenobligationen) with effect from Thursday, October 17.</p>
<p>SBC gave the following details:</p>
<p> Cash bonds	    New Rate	   Previous</p>
<p> Two-year		1.75 pct	   2.0 pct</p>
<p> Three-year	    2.25 pct	   2.5 pct</p>
<p> Four-year	     2.75 pct	   3.0 pct</p>
<p> Five-year	     3.0 pct	    3.25 pct</p>
<p> Six-year		3.25 pct	   3.50 pct</p>
<p> Seven-year	    3.5 pct	    3.75 pct</p>
<p> Eight-year	    3.75 pct	   4.0 pct</p>
<p>Note - Cash bonds, fixed-rate deposits for small investors, are used by banks to help finance their mortgage lending.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
